VIBRATO (vibrato) for the Elektron Octatrack MKI / MKII

VIBRATO was written by Bryan T (Bryan Tysinger, https://github.com/bryantysinger)
and contributed to the octabam project, where it was merged as pull request 1045
on 5 November 2026 (commit 960882f3), followed the same day by his SPD and DEP
glide (commit 0869753f). This copy is that module as on octabam main at
commit e85f54e0d570bd74bfd70b9d5467b35c01b9c468. It is distributed under
octabam's MIT License, whose full text follows unchanged and is also kept
byte for byte at upstream/LICENSE.

- The module (vibrato.asm, vibrato_ref.py, vibrato.dsp, its declaration in
  manifest.py, the render gate verify_vibrato.py,
  upstream/modules/vibrato/README.md, upstream/docs/vibrato-usage.md):
  Bryan T.
- The octabam SDK, schema and harness it is written against: Sam Banks.
- Modwerk's adaptations of vibrato.asm, manifest.py and verify_vibrato.py
  (listed in README.md and sdk/imports/vibrato-e85f54e.json), README.md,
  TESTING.md, octamod.module.json, media/ and presentation/thumbnail.svg are
  contributed under the same MIT terms.

No Elektron firmware, extracted stock routine or table is included. The
module reads the stock sine table from the unit's own DSP memory at run time.

